WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.210
Cost every plate, protect allergic guests, and get paid safely.

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:12.900
This is the video for module three of Catering Basics and Food Safety: costing, allergens and running a professional service.

3
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:21.700
Many home cooks price by feel, then finish a big job tired, with almost nothing left. The cure is a costing sheet.

4
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.930
Every naira you will spend, divided by the number of plates, plus the profit you choose.

5
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:32.180
You will also learn to protect guests with food allergies.

6
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.330
And to quote and take deposits like a professional.

7
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:44.710
Let us follow Ronke. These prices are approximate examples only. Use your own market prices on the day you quote.

8
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:56.650
Ingredients come to about 224,200 naira. Chicken alone is 126,000 of that, over 40 percent of the total.

9
00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:07.650
Then the hidden costs people forget. Gas, about 12,000. Packs, spoons and nylon for 110 packs, about 22,000.

10
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:14.590
Transport, about 15,000. And two helpers at 10,000 each, 20,000.

11
00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:29.330
The total job cost is 293,200 naira. Divided by 100 plates, each plate costs about 2,932 naira. Anything below that loses money.

12
00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:45.570
Markup is profit as a percentage of cost. Margin is profit as a percentage of the selling price. Mixing them up is why many caterers earn less than they think. To price with margin, divide the cost by 1 minus the margin.

13
00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:57.680
Ronke wants a 30% margin, so she divides 2,932 by 0.70. That gives 4,189 naira.

14
00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:09.830
She rounds to 4,200 per plate. For 100 plates, that is 420,000 naira, with about 126,800 profit.

15
00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:23.730
Market prices can rise before the event, so write that the quote is valid for 7 days. And pay yourself through a labour line, separate from profit. Never cut cost by cutting food safety.

16
00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:38.740
A food allergy can be severe and life-threatening, and cooking does not remove most allergens. Even a trace from a shared spoon can be enough. Groundnut hides in suya spice, kuli-kuli and some small chops.

17
00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:43.360
Ground crayfish hides in jollof, stews and egusi.

18
00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.620
Egg is in moi moi, puff puff and salad cream.

19
00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:53.570
And wheat is in meat pie, chin chin, and spring roll and samosa wrappers.

20
00:02:54.820 --> 00:03:05.480
Ask every client about allergies, and write the answer on the job sheet, not only in a chat. Halima's client said the bride's sister has a severe groundnut allergy.

21
00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:15.030
Halima checked every dish. The suya spice contains groundnut, and her chin chin is fried in the same oil as groundnut snacks.

22
00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:23.210
She cooked one pack first, before the kitchen was full of groundnut dust, with clean pots, spoons and fresh oil.

23
00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:31.360
She sealed it and labelled it, no groundnut, with the guest's name, and left out the chin chin she could not guarantee.

24
00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:48.050
She handed it to the client personally. If a guest asks and you are not sure, say: I am not sure, so please do not eat it. If someone has trouble breathing or swelling after eating, call for emergency help and get them to a hospital immediately.

25
00:03:49.300 --> 00:04:08.290
Ronke's quote of 420,000 naira asks for a 50% deposit, 210,000, before she buys any ingredient. The balance is due two days before the event. She confirms every payment in her banking app and sends a receipt with the amount, date and balance remaining.

26
00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:20.420
Fraudsters send fake SMS and screenshot alerts. Never trust them. Write your guest-count and cancellation terms on the quote, so they are agreed before any money moves.

27
00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:37.390
To remember. Count every cost and divide by the plates. Price with margin, not markup. Cook allergen-free meals first, sealed and labelled. Take a deposit before you shop. And confirm payments in your banking app, never by SMS alone.

28
00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:50.970
Now practise. Cost one menu package with current market prices. Write ingredient cards and mark the allergens. And create your quotation, event record and feedback message templates.

29
00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:53.260
Continue with the lessons below.
